def add(sub,block,title,why,facts,static,analysis,trap,mains,src='PRS',day=0,ap=False,p='P1',mag=False):
 extra=dict(magazine_edition='2026-06',magazine_posted='2026-07-31') if mag else {}
 J.append(dict(id=f'E13-2606-{len(J)+1:03}',date=f'2026-06-{day:02}' if day else '2026-06-30',date_precision='day' if day else 'month',subject=sub,block=block,title=title,why=why,facts=facts.split('|'),static_link=static,analysis=analysis.split('|'),trap=trap,mains=mains,priority=p,ap=ap,sources=['E13-'+x for x in src.split(',')],status='Historical June-indexed selected study note; not certification of latest law/data or completed implementation',checked='2026-11-07',evidence_access='Actual source reading and limits appear in the source-access registry. Static connections, analysis and exam guidance are original.',**extra))
add('Polity & Governance','01 · Federal river governance','Tungabhadra disputes: negotiation, adjudication and basin data','Vision’s June editorial article reports a proposed high-level mechanism for Andhra Pradesh, Telangana and Karnataka. Posting31July is not itself the event date.','Tungabhadra is formed by the Tunga and Bhadra and joins the Krishna as a right-bank tributary.|Upper Bhadra objections and Rajolibanda canal delivery problems concern different projects and cannot be reduced to one disputed reservoir.|Article262 empowers parliamentary adjudication legislation; StateList17 is subject to UnionList56.','The1956inter-state disputes law and River Boards Act have different institutional functions. Article263 consultation does not itself replace adjudication.','An AP answer should separate agreed allocation, measured inflows, sedimentation, operational releases and actual canal delivery.|Shared gauges, drought protocols, transparent accounts and ecological flow checks can reduce conflicts without prejudging legal shares.','The article’s recommendation to implement a2019Bill is not proof of enactment. Do not call the Cauvery authority a newly-created Tungabhadra board or certify pending court outcomes.','How can basin-level cooperation complement lawful water-dispute adjudication?',src='VISION',mag=True)
add('Polity & Governance','02 · Equal access to justice','DISHA2.0: four components, one access-to-justice objective','The22June approval restructures a central-sector scheme for2026–31.','The approved outlay is₹255crore, entirely through Union budgetary support.|Four components are Tele-Law, Nyaya Bandhu, legal literacy/awareness and the new VIDHI-Sanjeevani.|VIDHI-Sanjeevani envisages an integrated dashboard and multilingual Nyaya Setu chatbot; cumulative outreach target is three crore.','Article39A concerns equal justice and free legal aid; legal information, pre-litigation advice and court representation are not identical services.','For AP, assisted access in Telugu, confidentiality and referral to qualified counsel matter more than chatbot interactions alone.|Audit resolved problems, representation and accessibility; avoid treating repeated programme contacts as three crore distinct people receiving final remedies.','Tele-Law’s broad access to advice is not the same eligibility rule as representation under section12of the Legal Services Authorities Act.','Design a technology-assisted legal-aid system that remains accessible and accountable.',src='DISHA',day=22)
add('Polity & Governance','03 · Civil society regulation','FCRA amendments: utilisation, disclosure and proportionality','PRS reports the June amendments; the primary FCRA PDF could not be retrieved in this batch.','The review describes approved-purpose lists under religious,cultural,economic,educational and social categories.|Subsequent instalments require activity-wise disclosure,75%utilisation of the previous instalment and field inquiry.|The reviewed definition of reasonable activity uses at least₹10lakhforeign-contribution utilisation over the last two financial years.','FCRA registration/prior permission regulates foreign contribution; it is not a general licence required for every domestic charitable donation.','AP organisations need clear activity classification, timely records and proportionate compliance support.|For Mains, weigh transparency and prevention of diversion against administrative delays, small-organisation burdens and procedural fairness.','These details follow PRS, not independently read Gazette text. Do not treat a threshold as a guaranteed automatic cancellation without statutory process or review.','How can foreign-contribution oversight preserve both accountability and legitimate civic activity?',p='P2')
add('Economy','01 · National accounts — release and reference period','GDP provisional estimates:7.7%annual growth on the new base','MoSPI published the FY2025–26 provisional estimates on5June.','Real GDP growth is7.7%; nominal GDP growth is8.9%, using base2022–23.|Real GVA growth is7.9%; Q4realGDPgrowth is7.8%. These are different aggregates/periods.|Manufacturing GVA grew10.7%; the trade/transport-related grouping11.0%; financial/real-estate/professional services10.4%.','GDP at market prices equals GVA plus product taxes minus product subsidies. Real and nominal growth use different price treatments.','Use the June release to update earlier advance estimates, not relabel the whole financial year as June output.|For AP, national growth does not establish the state’s growth rate; state accounts need their own release,base and revision vintage.','A higher sectoral growth rate does not imply the largest absolute contribution. Do not splice old-base GDP levels into the rebased series.','What do GDP revisions reveal about both economic performance and statistical uncertainty?',src='GDP',day=5)
add('Economy','02 · Monetary policy — decision versus minutes','June MPC: unchanged rates, weaker growth and inflation risks','The meeting ran3–5June; the inspected document is its19June minutes, not a second meeting.','Repo remains5.25%, SDF5.00%, MSF and BankRate5.50%; the decision was unanimous.|The MPC retained a neutral stance; that is not a promise of the next rate cut.|FY2026–27realGDPgrowth is projected at6.6%, CPIinflation5.1%,coreinflation4.7%.','Repo is a policy rate; SDF absorbs liquidity without collateral. The statutory BankRate is not best defined simply as an ordinary long-term lending rate.','Energy-price pass-through and a deficient-monsoon risk create a supply-shock trade-off: raising rates cannot produce rain or oil.|Assess expectations,second-round effects and credit transmission; AP food exposure and irrigation conditions can differ from national averages.','Forecasts are not realised annual outcomes. Publication19June should not overwrite the5June decision date.','Why can a neutral MPC hold rates during simultaneous growth and inflation risks?',src='MPC',day=5)
add('Economy','03 · External accounts — net and gross flows','Q4 current-account surplus despite a goods deficit','RBI’s8June preliminary balance-of-payments release coversJanuary–March2026.','Q4current-account surplus isUS$7.1billion,0.7%ofGDP; goods balance is−US$83.4billion.|Net services are+US$60.4billion, primary income−US$11.1billion and secondary income+US$41.3billion.|Gross personal-transfer receipts areUS$43.5billion; the full-year current account remains in deficit atUS$25.2billion,0.6%ofGDP.','Current account includes goods,services,primary and secondary income; remittances are not simply the entire net secondary-income balance.','The rounded components reconcile to aboutUS$7.2billion, with the published7.1difference explained by rounding.|AP migration analysis should distinguish household remittances from portfolio flows and evaluate concentration and exchange-rate exposure.','Do not reproduce PRS’sUS$30.1billiontransfer shorthand or call a quarterly surplus a full-year surplus. FDI/FPI belong in financial-account analysis.','How do services and remittances cushion India’s external vulnerability?',src='BOP',day=8)
add('Economy','04 · Tax law — ordinance and deemed effect','Government-security tax exemption for FIIs and BIS','The5June Income-tax Amendment Ordinance is deemed effective from1April2026.','Ordinance2of2026amends ScheduleIVof the Income-tax Act,2025.|New entries cover government-security interest and capital gains on sale,exchange or transfer for a Foreign Institutional Investor and the Bank for International Settlements.|The exemption remains subject to furnishing prescribed information.','Article123ordinances have statutory force subject to constitutional legislative control. Deemed commencement can precede promulgation.','Assess how tax treatment may attract debt-market participation, while interest-rate,currency and exit risks remain.|For exam use distinguish FII/BIS eligibility from a universal exemption for every person or all securities.','The reviewed text concerns Government securities as defined by the2006Act, not all corporate bonds. Later replacement or lapse is not certified here.','Evaluate the benefits and risks of tax incentives for sovereign-debt investment.',src='TAX',day=5)
add('Economy','05 · Foreign portfolio investment','FEMA opens the individual route beyond NRI/OCI status','The12June non-debt-instrument amendment extends the specified listed-equity route to individuals resident outside India.','The residence-based category includes but is not limited to NRIs and OCIs.|The reviewed portfolio ceiling is below10%for an individual; aggregate holdings under the route are capped at24%.|Government-approval safeguards remain where a transaction transfers ownership/control to relevant land-border-country entities/citizens or covered beneficial owners.','FEMA residence, citizenship and OCI status are distinct legal concepts. FPI and FDI cannot be differentiated solely by a buyer’s nationality.','Broader participation may deepen markets,but beneficial-owner identification and consistent investor-group aggregation matter.|AP firms seeking finance should separate an overseas individual’s exchange purchase from greenfield investment or an industrial project commitment.','Exactly10%is not below10%. Do not read the reform as eliminating all sectoral,reporting or ownership-control safeguards.','How can India deepen foreign participation while preserving transparent ownership?',src='PRS,FEMA',day=12)
add('Economy','06 · Financial consumers — consent and suitability','Mis-selling rules: consent alone is insufficient','RBI issued15June directions with effect from1January2027.','Commercial-bank definitions treat a sale as mis-selling if unsuitable or inappropriate even where the customer explicitly consents.|Explicit consent must be informed and recorded; an interface’s default choice must beNo/I do not agree.|Banks must distinguish third-party sellers from staff and preserve consent records; the framework addresses deceptive designs and compulsory bundling.','Consumer autonomy includes suitability, truthful disclosure and a genuine ability to refuse, not merely an OTP or signed form.','AP financial-literacy programmes should train customers to separate deposits,insurance and investment products and identify the provider and risk.|Supervision should test incentive structures, complaint outcomes and accessible cancellation, not only consent-box completion.','Issued inJune does not mean these new directions were operative inJune. Other bank/NBFCcategories have separate companion instruments.','Why is explicit consent necessary but not sufficient for fair financial selling?',src='SALE',day=15)
add('Economy','07 · Digital fraud — liability allocation','Digital-fraud liability: bank burden and a calendar-day clock','The24June directions apply to electronic transactions undertaken on or after1January2027.','The bank bears the burden of proving customer liability; bank negligence attracts zero customer liability.|Third-party breach attracts zero liability if reported to the bank within five calendar days from occurrence.|Where customer negligence is established,the customer normally bears pre-reporting loss subject to eligible compensation; post-reporting unauthorised loss is borne by the bank.','Bank deficiency,third-party breach and customer negligence are distinct categories. Approval under coercion can still fall within the reviewed fraudulent-transaction definition.','Grievance systems need24×7reporting, immediate acknowledgement and rapid prevention of further fraud.|The directions set maximum examination/response timelines of45calendar days for domestic complaints and60for cross-border complaints.','The five-day clock is from occurrence,not five working days after reading an SMS. A complaint does not automatically establish negligence or guarantee full reimbursement.','Design a liability framework that protects victims without rewarding weak security.',src='FRAUD',day=24)
add('Economy','08 · Small-fraud compensation — eligibility and arithmetic','Fraud compensation: gross threshold,net-loss calculation and sunset','The same24June directions create a limited compensation mechanism for specified bona fide victims.','Eligible complaints involve gross loss up to₹50,000; compensation is the lower of85%of net loss and₹25,000.|The victim must report to both the bank and1930/cybercrime portal within five calendar days; eligibility includes a bona fide determination.|The benefit is once in a lifetime; the mechanism covers qualifying losses occurring up to one year from the directions’ effective date.','Gross loss determines the threshold,while net loss deducts recoveries. This mechanism addresses specified customer-negligence cases,not a universal replacement for zero-liability rules.','Example:₹40,000gross loss with₹15,000recovered leaves₹25,000net loss; eligible compensation is₹21,250.|Public messaging in AP should preserve reporting duties,one-time use and the limited time window rather than promise an automatic₹25,000payment.','Neither every₹50,000loss gets85%nor every fraud qualifies. Do not omit the one-year loss window or confuse it with the lifetime claim limit.','How should temporary fraud relief balance financial inclusion, incentives and fiscal exposure?',src='FRAUD',day=24)
add('Economy','09 · Insolvency — liquidation supervision','Liquidation reform: creditor oversight and shorter clocks','The amendment is dated1June; the inspected Gazette bears2June and publication-based commencement.','The committee of creditors supervises liquidation with prescribed prior-approval requirements.|The amended liquidation timeline is180days instead of one year; distribution after receipt is shortened from90to15days.|Selected English provisions require at least66%voting share for specified recommendations/actions; the Adjudicating Authority remains relevant.','Corporate resolution seeks a viable plan; liquidation realises/distributes assets. Committee oversight does not make all creditors equally ranked.','Faster distribution can limit value erosion,but rushed sales and poor valuations can reduce recoveries.|AP MSME suppliers need clear claims assistance and realistic recovery expectations; a statutory clock does not guarantee full payment.','Do not date every provision’s operation1June solely from the signature or say the liquidator’s duties vanish while an extension application is undecided.','Can creditor-led liquidation improve speed without sacrificing fairness?',src='PRS,IBBI')
add('Economy','10 · Aviation — recoverable stabilisation finance','ATF stabilisation:₹10,000crore is an advance,not a permanent grant','The3June Cabinet decision supports willing scheduled Indian airlines through OMCs.','Interest-free advances up to₹10,000crore compensate OMCs under the benchmark-price mechanism.|As international prices moderate,the differential is recovered and returned to the Consolidated Fund of India.|Participating airlines procure ATF only from OMCs under the arrangement; normal duration is36months with annual review or earlier full recovery.','Price smoothing redistributes volatility across time and actors; it does not remove the underlying import cost or automatically fix every airfare.','For AP aviation expansion, distinguish airport infrastructure and route viability from temporary national fuel support.|Audit benchmark setting,claims,recoveries and competitive effects; competent-authority extension is possible if the corpus remains untrued-up.','Do not call this debt forgiveness for airlines or an unconditional₹10,000crorefare subsidy. International as well as domestic operations are covered.','Evaluate temporary fuel-price smoothing as a response to external shocks.',src='ATF',day=3)
add('Economy','11 · Industrial statistics — launch chronology','IIP rebasing: actual launch on1June,not a May calendar slot','The later MoSPI29June release explicitly identifies the initial new-series release as1June.','The revised IIPseries uses base2022–23; the earlier calendar’s28May date was a schedule,not the actual launch.|A release date differs from the reference month whose production is measured.|Rebasing changes basket,weights and methods; compare growth within a consistent series and vintage.','IIP measures industrial production rather than the whole economy; GDP/GVA include services and other sectors with different coverage.','AP industrial analysis should compare sector composition and physical/value-based measurement rather than infer state output from an all-India index.|Keep a revision log so a newer series replaces rather than silently mixes with an older chart.','Do not present June actual-release evidence as a May outcome or assume identical index levels across different base years.','Why does a statistical rebase require careful communication as well as new data?',src='IIP',day=1)
add('Economy','12 · Industrial statistics — price deflation','29June IIP: PPI-based supersession is a second milestone','The29June release supersedes the first new-series estimates with the revised price treatment.','The inspected release identifies234of463value-based item groups with36.02%weight for the relevant deflation treatment.|Value-based observations need price adjustment to infer volume; an observed rise in sales value need not equal real output growth.|A later methodological revision differs from routine inclusion of late factory returns.','A producer-price measure and consumer inflation represent different stages and baskets; they are not interchangeable simply because both are price indices.','For answers, connect better producer-price deflation to more credible industrial volume estimates.|Flag breaks in comparability and preserve the release vintage; do not add physical-output series and nominal turnover without common units.','Do not date PPI-based supersession1June or mistake36.02%weight for36.02%industrial growth.','How can improved price deflation change interpretation of industrial performance?',src='IIP',day=29)
add('Agriculture','01 · Food entitlement — consultation,not enactment','Draft AAY formula:7kgper person with a35kghousehold ceiling','DFPD’s public consultation sought comments until13July2026.','The existing reviewed AAY entitlement is35kgper household per month; priority households use5kgper person.|The draft proposes7kgper AAY person per month but retains a maximum35kgper household.|A three-person AAY household would receive21kgunder the draft formula; five persons reach35kgand larger families remain capped.','The NFSA2013is distinct from the Food Safety and Standards Act. A draft’s enactment wording is standard drafting,not proof Parliament passed it.','The cap weakens any claim that per-capita equalisation solves deprivation in large households; small households can lose grain relative to35kg.|AP evaluation needs household-size distribution, appeals and nutrition evidence rather than announcing increased grain for every AAYfamily.','Do not omit the35kgcap or treat consultation as a changed current entitlement. Later enactment/notification remains unchecked.','Critically examine household caps in a proposed per-person food entitlement.',src='NFSA')
add('Society & Welfare','01 · Medical devices — risk-based regulation','Draft device licensing: speed should not dilute risk scrutiny','PRS records a23June consultation on the Medical Devices Rules2017.','The proposal shortens licensing and intermediate-stage timelines for ClassesB,CandD.|Risk classes progress from low-riskAto high-riskD; product-specific classification matters.|The consultation deadline was23July2026; this batch has not verified a final notification.','Devices and medicines both involve health regulation but their risk classifications and licensing pathways are not identical.','AP’s medical-device manufacturing ecosystem needs predictable timelines alongside testing,quality management and post-market surveillance.|Shorter administrative processing can help investment; it does not establish the safety of every product or remove regulator accountability.','Do not describe a draft as an operative exemption or assume all devices,includingClassA,share the same revised schedule.','How should risk-based licensing reconcile timely access and patient safety?',p='P2')
add('Society & Welfare','02 · Drug imports — remaining shelf life','Draft drug rule: one-year residual life with explicit exceptions','The June consultation proposes a change to import shelf-life requirements.','The reviewed existing rule uses more than60%remaining shelf life at import.|The draft proposes a minimum one-year residual life for drugs generally.|Biological products and radiopharmaceuticals retain the60%criterion; comments were invited until22July.','A percentage-of-original-life threshold and an absolute-time threshold can produce different results depending on the product’s total shelf life.','Procurement in AP should consider cold chain,expiry risk,clinical demand and stock rotation,not only purchase price.|Short-lived imaging agents and vaccines illustrate why exceptions matter; neither rule alone ensures quality after poor storage.','Do not say the one-year proposal applies without exception or that remaining life is measured from patient use rather than the specified import stage.','What safeguards should accompany changes in drug-import shelf-life rules?',p='P2')
add('Society & Welfare','03 · Emergency medicine — dispatch and outcomes','National Ambulance Services: transport plus pre-hospital care','The29June guidelines release emphasises standardisation,triage and integrated dispatch.','The framework covers ambulance categories,staffing,medicines,equipment,maintenance and training.|Ambulances are to conform toAIS-125; GPS-based tracking and Integrated Command and Dispatch Centres support coordination.|GIS planning includes referral capacity,bed readiness,accident hotspots and geographic constraints;112integration is progressive.','The nearest hospital is not always the nearest appropriate facility. Response time,stabilisation and handover all influence survival.','For AP, analyse hill/tribal access and highway trauma with fleet availability,trained EMTs and receiving-hospital readiness.|Report call-to-dispatch,arrival,referral completion and patient outcomes; vehicle purchases alone do not establish equitable service.','Guidelines and proposed integration are not proof every state fleet already meets every norm or every call routes through112.','Design an equitable, data-informed emergency transport network.',src='NAS',day=29)
add('Society & Welfare','04 · Climate and household vulnerability','Climate shocks are also a cost-of-living problem','Selected June-compilation passages connect heat,food,water and household costs.','Heat can increase cooling expenditure while reducing safe working hours.|Rainfall shocks can affect farm output,food logistics and household purchasing power.|Water scarcity and illness can add tanker,healthcare and lost-wage costs beyond a headline consumer basket.','Distribution matters: the same price rise imposes a larger burden on a household spending most income on essentials.','AP responses can combine cool roofs,drinking water,work-rest protocols,public health surveillance and drought-resilient agriculture.|Separate magazine recommendations for new authorities/laws from existing institutions; assess fiscal incidence and service quality.','Do not copy the compilation’s older45.86%CPIfood weight into the rebased2024series or attribute all food inflation to climate alone.','How should climate adaptation protect household real incomes?',src='DRISHTI',p='P2')
add('International Relations','01 · France — innovation and economic security','India–France: technology cooperation beyond procurement','PRS reports the June roadmap and associated initiatives.','Areas include critical technologies,innovation,research and talent mobility.|Initiatives include AIcooperation,aeronautics skilling,digital sciences and an Economic Security Dialogue.|The review also records a classified-information security agreement and an ambition to double bilateral trade in five years.','A roadmap,MoUand a binding treaty have different legal effects; a trade target is not a realised flow.','AP’s aerospace and university ecosystem can analyse skills,testing capacity and supplier linkages without claiming a nationalMoUalready funds a state centre.|Assess technology absorption,IPterms,export controls and research mobility rather than count announcements alone.','No bilateral announcement guarantees unrestricted transfer of every sensitive technology or immediate doubling of trade.','How can strategic partnerships build domestic technological capability?',p='P2')
add('International Relations','02 · Myanmar — security and neighbourhood','India–Myanmar talks: connectivity amid difficult political conditions','The visit straddled lateMay and earlyJune; June’s review records its outcomes.','The two sides discussed trade,connectivity,defence and border security.|India reiterated support for Myanmar’s sovereignty and cooperation against cross-border threats.|Implementation faces conflict,displacement and security constraints distinct from the wording of a joint statement.','Neighbourhood diplomacy intersects humanitarian concerns,transnational crime and infrastructure reliability; engagement does not settle every domestic legitimacy question.','Analyse the Kaladan/Northeast connectivity context while distinguishing a corridor commitment from functioning end-to-end transit.|AP ports’ widerBayofBengalcommercial interest is an analytical connection,not proof of a new JuneAPshipping service.','Do not label a multi-day visit whollyJune or infer announced connectivity is already safe,complete and routinely used.','How should India balance security,humanitarian and connectivity interests in Myanmar?',p='P2')
add('International Relations','03 · Mauritius — partnership and delivery','India–Mauritius: judge a package by project outcomes','PRS records the June review of the enhanced strategic partnership.','Leaders reviewed progress under an India-supported special economic package.|Mauritius is an IndianOceanpartner with maritime,development and people-to-people links.|A package can contain multiple projects and financing arrangements whose terms need separate verification.','Development assistance,grants,concessional credit and commercial investment are different flows; a headline package is not immediate expenditure.','Study strategic partnership through project selection,local priorities,maintenance and transparent procurement.|For AP comparative answers,connect maritime skills and blue-economy opportunity without inventing a signed state-level agreement.','Do not add a reviewed package to fresh commitments as though all amounts are new or treat diplomatic reassurance as completed implementation.','How can development partnerships support resilient Indian Ocean cooperation?',p='P2')
add('International Relations','04 · Seychelles — multiple legal instruments','Seychelles: five MoUs are not the entire agreement set','PRS records digital,maritime,space and financing outcomes.','The fiveMoUscover diplomatic training,digital payments,agricultural research,recognition of seafarer certification and space.|An extradition treaty and umbrella infrastructure line-of-credit agreement are separate instruments.|Recognition of training can support mobility,but credential scope and domestic rules still matter.','An MoUcount does not equal the total number of instruments. A credit line is financing,not necessarily a grant or immediate disbursement.','For AP maritime training,consider standards,employment contracts,seafarer welfare and skills recognition as a complete chain.|Assess project debt sustainability and local demand rather than assume every new credit commitment yields productive assets.','Do not call the extradition treaty one of the fiveMoUsor claim operationalUPIacceptance everywhere from a digital-paymentsMoUalone.','Why should maritime partnerships integrate skills,governance and infrastructure?',p='P2')
add('International Relations','05 · Slovakia — comprehensive partnership','India–Slovakia: a wider European partnership portfolio','The June review records elevation to a comprehensive partnership.','SixMoUsinclude labour migration,digital technologies,higher education,audio-visual creation,quantum communication/critical infrastructure and naturopathy.|Other reviewed instruments address defence,student exchanges and tourism.|A counter-terrorism working group and consular dialogue were announced.','A comprehensive partnership is a diplomatic framework,not automatic free movement or a free-trade agreement.','AP learners and firms should distinguish a mobilityMoUfrom recognised qualifications,visas and enforceable employment protection.|Technology collaboration needs research teams,IParrangements and financing; an announced quantum link is not evidence a secure network is commissioned.','Do not substituteSloveniaforSlovakiaor treat bilateral instruments as binding allEUmember states.','How can diversified European partnerships support India’s skills and technology goals?',p='P2')
add('International Relations','06 · Antarctic governance — anniversary and treaty layers','Antarctic Treaty:65years since entry into force','The public June compilation marks23June1961entry into force.','The Treaty was signed1December1959and entered into force23June1961.|Its geographic scope is south of60°S; peaceful purposes and scientific cooperation are central.|Territorial claims are held in abeyance; the environmental protocol and marine-living-resources convention form separate layers of the broader system.','Treaty signature,entry into force and later protocols are different milestones. Military personnel/equipment for permitted peaceful purposes are not simply banned in every circumstance.','Analyse scientific freedom alongside tourism pressure,ecosystem protection and geopolitical competition.|India’s polar research can strengthen climate knowledge,but Antarctica is not the Arctic and a station does not confer territorial sovereignty.','Do not say the Treaty was signed in1961or that the environmental protocol automatically expires in2048.','How can science-based cooperation protect Antarctic governance?',src='DRISHTI',day=23,p='P2')
add('International Relations','07 · Defence logistics and strategic autonomy','Logistics agreements: access does not equal permanent basing','June’s compilation revisits India’s logistics-support arrangements; this is a thematic supplement,not a newly-signed June treaty claim.','Logistics support can cover refuelling,replenishment,repairs and agreed services.|Reciprocal arrangements can support exercises,port calls and humanitarian assistance.|Actual access depends on agreed scope,consent and operational procedures; it is not a blanket alliance commitment.','Logistics endurance and combat authorisation are distinct. A facility visit does not transfer sovereignty over the host’s base.','AP maritime analysis can connect longer on-station endurance to eastern-seaboard logistics and disaster response.|Assess reimbursement,information protection and partner reliability; no newVisakhapatnambasing commitment is established here.','Country counts,personnel caps and the compilation’sJanuaryRELOSoperationalisation claim remain primary-text unchecked and are not tested as settled facts.','How can logistics cooperation expand reach while preserving strategic autonomy?',src='DRISHTI',p='P2')
add('Environment','01 · Biochar — mitigation with conditions','Biochar: soil benefits need feedstock and lifecycle scrutiny','Selected June passages revisit crop-residue pyrolysis as an alternative to open burning.','Biochar is a carbon-rich porous material produced by heating biomass with limited oxygen.|Potential benefits include water/nutrient retention and a more persistent soil-carbon pool.|Outcomes depend on feedstock,production conditions,soil,crop and application rate; generic percentage yield gains are not universal.','Pyrolysis is not complete combustion or anaerobic digestion. Carbon storage requires attention to stability,additionality and lifecycle emissions.','AP paddy-residue and horticultural systems need field trials,contaminant testing,safe emissions control and viable collection costs.|Do not divert residues from essential fodder/soil uses or assume every biomass input is sustainably sourced.','Biochar is not automatically zero-emission,permanent or equally beneficial in every soil. Avoid universalising selected trial percentages.','What safeguards make biochar a credible circular-agriculture intervention?',src='DRISHTI',p='P2')
add('Environment','02 · Coral stress and resilience','Bleached coral is stressed,not necessarily dead','The compilation discusses climate-resilient reef identification and restoration priorities.','Coral bleaching involves loss of symbiotic algae or pigments and can follow thermal or other stress.|Corals are animals; many reef-building corals rely on photosynthetic symbionts.|Recovery is possible if conditions improve,but prolonged stress can cause mortality.','Resilience means a relative capacity to resist/recover,not immunity to warming,acidification,pollution or repeated marine heatwaves.','Conservation should combine local water quality,fishery management and climate mitigation with monitoring.|For AP coastal comparison,do not relocateLakshadweeporAndamanreef systems to the mainland merely to manufacture a state connection.','Bleaching and mortality are not synonymous; an identified resilient reef does not prove all corals there tolerate any future temperature.','Why is local reef conservation necessary but insufficient under ocean warming?',src='DRISHTI',p='P2')
add('Environment','03 · Desertification and watershed governance','17June: land restoration is more than planting trees','The June compilation links the observance with watershed-development activities.','Desertification is land degradation in arid,semi-arid and dry sub-humid areas,not simply expansion of sandy deserts.|Watershed measures can reduce erosion,improve infiltration and support farming/livelihoods.|Restoration needs community maintenance,water budgeting and suitable vegetation rather than plantation counts alone.','UNCCDland-degradation neutrality concerns balancing losses with restoration while avoiding degradation first. Watersheds follow drainage,not necessarily district borders.','ForRayalaseema,combine crop choice,soil moisture,commons restoration and groundwater demand management.|Recharge works cannot sustain unlimited extraction; evaluate downstream flows and the distribution of benefits to landless households.','Do not treat every degraded hectare as a desert or infer higher groundwater levels from the number of structures sanctioned.','How can watershed governance support both ecological restoration and rural incomes?',src='DRISHTI',day=17,p='P2')
add('Environment','04 · Climate research capacity','Climate instruments: calibration is part of scientific self-reliance','Selected passages discuss theMegaScienceVision2035climate-research review.','Measurement instruments,calibration and maintenance determine the quality of climate observations.|Earth-system models require regional data and validation; imported instruments alone do not guarantee accurate local forecasts.|The compilation reports concerns and recommendations,not a law that all imported instruments are prohibited.','Scientific independence is reproducibility and capability,not isolation from international research or a ban on collaboration.','AP universities can link reliable coastal/weather observations to agriculture,cyclone preparedness and heat-health planning.|Support procurement flexibility with quality controls,reference standards,open metadata and trained technicians.','A model adapted from another country is not automatically invalid; performance must be evaluated. Do not present a recommendation as an operating procurement exemption.','Why should climate resilience include investment in measurement science?',src='DRISHTI',p='P2')
add('Environment','05 · Sand mining and river habitats','Chambal scrutiny: extraction needs replenishment evidence','June’s compilation reports judicial concern over illegal mining in the tri-stateChambalsanctuary.','The riverine protected area spansRajasthan,MadhyaPradesh andUttarPradesh.|Sand extraction can alter riverbeds,bank stability,nesting sites and groundwater interactions.|Gharials,dolphins,turtles and riverine birds depend on habitat conditions; protected status is not evidence that illegal activity is absent.','Minor-mineral administration,environmental clearance and wildlife protection are separate obligations. A lease is not a blanket exemption from the other safeguards.','AP river-sand governance can combine credible district surveys,replenishment studies,transport traceability and independent enforcement.|Manufactured sand can reduce some pressure,but quarrying,energy use and quality standards still require scrutiny.','The original court order was not read; no exact directions,current-case status or universal mining ban is certified.','How should construction demand be reconciled with river-system protection?',src='DRISHTI',p='P2')
add('Environment','06 · Biodiversity evidence and species rediscovery','Dragonfly rediscovery: observation is not population recovery','Selected June passages describe the long-tailed duskhawker and regionalOdonatarecords.','Dragonflies and damselflies belong toOdonata,with aquatic immature stages and terrestrial/aerial adults.|A rediscovery establishes a verified observation after a recording gap,not necessarily that a species was extinct.|Distribution,abundance,conservation assessment and survey effort measure different things.','Bioindicator value depends on species ecology and sampling methods; not every dragonfly tolerates the same water conditions.','AP wetland surveys can build seasonal baseline records,validate identifications and protect breeding habitat.|Avoid turning one specimen or a national species total into proof of healthy ecosystems everywhere.','Global/species counts vary with taxonomy and date; the compilation’s exact totals are not treated as a current official checklist.','Why should biodiversity reporting distinguish rediscovery,abundance and recovery?',src='DRISHTI',p='P3')
add('Environment','07 · Environmental mobilisation and outcomes','World Environment Day: assess survival,not only saplings','The public June compilation links5June observance with a tree-planting campaign.','WorldEnvironmentDay is observed5June and coordinated byUNEP.|TheEkPedMaaKeNaamcampaign was launched in2024; later achievements are not a new campaign launch.|Tree planting,restored natural forest and measured additional carbon storage are distinct indicators.','Articles48Aand51A(g)create environmental responsibilities at different constitutional levels; a campaign pledge is not itself an individual carbon credit.','AP programmes should select native species,protect grasslands and water budgets,and finance multi-year care.|Report survival,biodiversity and land tenure alongside planting numbers; avoid replacing established ecosystems with inappropriate monocultures.','The2026theme/host and specific plantation totals follow an unverified magazine lead and are omitted from factual recall questions.','How can mass environmental campaigns produce durable ecological gains?',src='DRISHTI',day=5,p='P2')
add('Science & Technology','01 · Particle physics — evidence and chronology','Jet quenching in light ions: a June result from2025collisions','ATLAS’s28June briefing reports oxygen–oxygen and neon–neon observations.','The analysed collisions were recorded in summer2025; publication and experiment dates differ.|Jet quenching means energetic partons lose energy while traversing the produced medium; dijet momentum imbalance is a measured signature.|The briefing reports central-collision observations exceeding the five-standard-deviation threshold,with weaker effects in peripheral collisions.','Quark–gluon plasma contains deconfined quarks/gluons and can behave as a low-viscosity fluid; it is not an ordinary gas or nuclear-fusion fuel.','The result helps examine how medium effects change with system size; oxygen/neonbridge smaller and heavier systems.|For science answers explain measurement,comparison and uncertainty rather than claiming researchers recreated the entireBigBang.','The2026announcement is not the first oxygen collision; low viscosity is not proof of exactly zero viscosity or unlimited stability.','What makes light-ion experiments useful for studying strongly interacting matter?',src='ATLAS,DRISHTI',day=28,p='P2')
add('Science & Technology','02 · Outbreak surveillance and international health','Bundibugyo: June update,May emergency determination','WHO’s8June report provides dated surveillance and response evidence.','WHO records534confirmed cases and93deaths acrossDRCandUganda as of6June; this is a historical snapshot.|A5JuneAfricaCDC–WHOresponse plan soughtUS$518million; funding requested is not funding received.|ThePHEICdetermination was17May,not a newJune declaration; the update warns that testing backlogs affect reported case increases.','Case-fatality ratios among detected cases are not infection-fatality estimates; surveillance completeness and reporting delays affect comparisons.','ForAPpreparedness,focus on port-of-entry coordination,clinical recognition,protective care and trustworthy risk communication rather than implying local cases.|Imported cases,linked secondary transmission and sustained community transmission are different epidemiological situations.','Do not label every newly confirmed case a newly acquired infection or presentJune counts as currentNovember totals.','How should outbreak communication balance vigilance with accurate risk assessment?',src='WHO,DRISHTI',day=8)
add('Agriculture','02 · Plant breeding and herbicide stewardship','IMI-resistant mustard: breeding method is not a safety verdict','The public compilation discusses proposedRabi2026–27cultivation of mutation-bred herbicide-tolerant mustard.','Mutation breeding induces variation and then selects useful traits; it differs from insertion of a transgene.|The discussedIMIresistance concerns herbicide tolerance and theALSpathway; resistance does not mean every weed is controlled forever.|The cultivation schedule and varietal approvals remain primary-source unchecked in this batch.','Herbicide-tolerant crop traits and drought tolerance are different. Mutation breeding,transgenesis and genome editing are not a simple two-box classification of all biotechnology.','Assess resistant-weed evolution,residue management,extension advice and non-chemical options before scaling.|APoilseed strategy must evaluate agronomic suitability rather than transplant a northernIndiaweed-management claim to every district.','Do not equate non-transgenic with risk-free or claim all genetic modification necessarily inserts DNAfrom another species.','How should agricultural innovation be paired with responsible herbicide use?',src='DRISHTI',p='P2')
add('Science & Technology','03 · Digital capability — inputs versus outcomes','Technology ecosystems: compute is an input,not an adoption metric','The June compilation surveysAI,quantum,cloud,biotechnology and skilling programmes.','Compute capacity,datasets,trained researchers and secure connectivity are complementary inputs.|Registration,enrolment,completion and job placement are different stages of a skills pipeline.|An approved mission’s outlay is not the same as expenditure or independently evaluated economic impact.','AGPUcount does not by itself describe usable compute: memory,networking,availability,price and task requirements matter.','APquantum/deep-tech initiatives need trained teams,research access,power reliability and accountable procurement.|Evaluate measurable public-use cases,model safety and local problem-solving rather than duplicate national headline commitment totals.','The compilation’s fast-changing programme counts are not reproduced as a verified current inventory or evidence ofAPdeployment.','How should public technology investment be evaluated beyond capacity announcements?',src='DRISHTI',p='P2')
add('Security','01 · Counter-drone preparedness','Rogue drones: layered detection and safe response','June’s public compilation revisits low-cost autonomous and remotely piloted threats.','Drones can support surveillance,logistics and attacks; platform size and operating altitude affect detectability.|RFdetection,radar,electro-optical tracking and authorised countermeasures have different strengths/limitations.|Jamming is not equally effective against all control modes and can interfere with legitimate systems.','Civilian drone regulation and military counter-drone operations have different authority,safety and proportionality requirements.','APports,airports and energy infrastructure need threat assessment,inter-agency command and tested response protocols.|Plan for false alarms,collateral risks and forensic evidence; expensive interceptors alone may not be a scalable answer to cheap swarms.','No single detector provides guaranteed coverage or legal authority to jam anywhere. Public demonstrations are not proof of universal battlefield effectiveness.','Design a proportionate layered defence against rogue-drone threats.',src='DRISHTI')
add('Security','02 · Critical infrastructure — IT/OT dependencies','Critical infrastructure: cyber failure can become physical harm','Selected June passages examine interconnectedIT,OTandIoTnetworks.','Operational technology controls physical processes such as grid switching,water treatment and industrial machinery.|Remote connectivity can expose old industrial systems to new attack paths.|Shared power,telecom and cloud dependencies can transmit disruption across sectors.','Critical information infrastructure is a legal/governance concept; not every connected device is automatically a formally notified protected system.','AP utilities need asset inventories,segmentation,secure remote access,vendor assurance and practised manual recovery.|Balance continuity with patching and safety engineering; a checklist audit or air-gap claim does not establish resilience.','Do not repeat the compilation’s unverified national legacy-system percentages or imply commercially useful quantum computers already break all encryption.','Why must infrastructure cybersecurity include engineering and recovery capacity?',src='DRISHTI')
add('Culture & History','01 · Conservation and public access','Heritage governance: visitor amenities are not ownership transfer','The June compilation reviews conservation,tourism and digital documentation initiatives.','Archaeological conservation,visitor facilities and tourism promotion have distinct objectives.|CSR-supported amenities do not by themselves transfer title or archaeological authority to a sponsor.|Digital archives improve access,but physical conservation,metadata and provenance remain necessary.','Monument protection,antiquities regulation,UNESCOlisting and manuscript preservation are not a single interchangeable designation.','AP’sAmaravatiandBuddhistheritage can support education and livelihoods when site carrying capacity and local participation guide development.|Evaluate accessibility,authenticity and conservation condition rather than only visitor footfall or commercial revenue.','No exhaustive current monument count or newly approvedAPheritage project is claimed from this retrospective overview.','How can heritage-led development protect authenticity and community interests?',src='DRISHTI',p='P2')
add('Culture & History','02 · Yoga — annual observance and public health','International Day of Yoga:12thobservance on21June2026','The public compilation discusses the2026observance and nationwide participation initiatives.','TheUNGeneralAssemblydeclared21Juneas theInternationalDayofYogain2014; the first observance was2015.|Counting2015as the first makes2026the12thobservance,not the12thanniversary of the first event.|Yoga encompasses physical,mental and philosophical traditions; a mass session is not a clinical efficacy trial.','Patanjali’s eight-limbed framework is not identical to every modern exercise routine. Cultural recognition and medical claims require different evidence.','APpublic-health outreach should be inclusive,adapted to age/disability and clear that exercise complements rather than replaces necessary care.|Distinguish registration,attendance and sustained practice; do not treat portal enrolments as audited participants.','The compilation’s2026theme and registration counts were not independently verified and are not included in tested recall.','How can cultural wellness initiatives support inclusive,evidence-informed public health?',src='DRISHTI',day=21,p='P2')
add('Culture & History','03 · Freedom movement — regional personalities','V.V.S.Aiyar: revolutionary networks and Tamil writing','June’s compilation notes his3June1925death anniversary.','V.V.S.Aiyar was associated withIndiaHouseand revolutionary networks inLondon.|He later worked fromFrenchPondicherry,linking nationalist activity and Tamil literary production.|He died3June1925;2026marks101years after his death,not a centenary.','The freedom struggle used transnational networks,regional-language journalism and multiple political methods; a single label cannot capture every phase of a person’s work.','ForAPPSCcomparison,study networks and print culture across the southern presidencies without conflatingAiyarwithV.O.ChidambaramPillaiorother similarly named leaders.|Separate documented biography from unverified claims about secret operations and precise authorship.','No complete primary biography or literary catalogue was read; avoid turning every magazine anecdote into a settled fact.','How did regional-language writing and overseas networks interact in the freedom struggle?',src='DRISHTI',day=3,p='P3')
add('Society & Welfare','05 · Prisons — capacity and constitutional rights','Prison overcrowding: national averages conceal local stress','The compilation reportsNCRBPrisonStatisticsIndia2024; the primary report remains unread.','Occupancy compares inmates with sanctioned capacity; it differs from a conviction rate.|Undertrials have not been convicted in the pending case; detention is not a finding of guilt.|Staffing,medical care,legal aid and release-order execution affect conditions alongside prison buildings.','Articles21and39Aanchor dignity and access to justice. BNSSbail provisions have eligibility conditions and exceptions,not unconditional release for every undertrial.','APanalysis should combine jail-wise capacity,legal aid,healthcare and timely court coordination.|Assess bail affordability and rehabilitation; adding beds alone can leave unnecessary detention and medical vacancies unaddressed.','The compilation’s112.7%national occupancy figure is secondary-reporting only; no primary-certified current prison table is claimed.','Why should prison decongestion be treated as a justice-system reform?',src='DRISHTI',p='P2')
add('Society & Welfare','06 · Language and education — practical federalism','Three-language policy: local capacity and minority rights','Selected June passages describe implementation concerns in multilingualNagaland.','NEP2020supports multilingualism and flexibility; at least two of the three languages are to be native toIndia.|Mother-tongue instruction and a particular three-language subject combination are separate policy questions.|Teacher supply,textbooks,script diversity and learning continuity shape feasibility.','Article350Aconcerns primary-stage mother-tongue instruction for linguistic minority children; theEighthScheduleis not a list of every language entitled to cultural protection.','APschools should considerTelugu,minority and tribal-language needs with genuine parental information and trained teachers.|Consultation and phased capacity building can protect learning without portraying every multilingual choice as a threat to integration.','A policy framework is not proof a particularCBSEcircular applies identically to every state-school board or mandatesHindiin all circumstances.','How can language policy reconcile integration,choice and educational inclusion?',src='DRISHTI',p='P2')
add('Andhra Pradesh','01 · Aviation policy — approval and ambition','AP Aviation Policy2026–31: distinguish policy period from2035targets','PTIreports the4JuneCabinetapproval.','The policy seeks airport/connectivity expansion and aerospace/MROinvestment.|Reported2035targets include passenger-handling capacity30.38million and cargo capacity4.27lakhtonnes.|The report envisages nine new airports and ten waterdromes; these are plans,not commissioned assets.','Passenger capacity,actual annual passengers and route frequency are different indicators. MROis maintenance,repair and overhaul,not airport ownership.','APshould evaluate demand,land,environment,airspace,skills and financial viability for each facility.|Connect nationalATFsmoothing to airline costs without claiming it guarantees all proposedAProutes or eliminates state infrastructure costs.','The policy’s2026–31title does not mean every2035target is due by2031; do not count planned airports as operational.','How shouldAPbalance regional access and viability in aviation expansion?',src='APCAB',day=4,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','02 · Polavaram canals — sanction versus delivery','Polavaram Left Main Canal: revised sanction is not irrigation achieved','The4JuneCabinetreport covers packages5and5A.','Reported works include excavation,embankment formation,lining and related infrastructure.|The described reach is roughlykm93.7–111; it is not the entirePolavaramproject.|Administrative sanction,contracts,physical completion and reliable delivered water are separate stages.','Irrigation outcomes depend on source availability,conveyance,distribution and farm-level access; a lined canal alone does not ensure equitable supply.','Assess land/access disputes,drainage,safety and tail-end delivery with transparent milestones.|ThePTIfigure₹796crorediffers from aHindu₹797crorerounding lead; avoid exact recall until a primary sanction is reconciled.','Do not add a revised package sanction to its previous sanction as entirely new spending or call all command-area benefits realised.','How can canal investments be evaluated by dependable and equitable water delivery?',src='APCAB',day=4,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','03 · Judicial infrastructure — complementary capacity','Amaravati High Court external works: buildings versus justice outcomes','The4JuneCabinetreport records₹547croreadministrative sanction.','The reported scope includes roads,parking,security pavilions,substations,water bodies and related external infrastructure.|External development is not the same scope as every court-building construction cost.|An administrative sanction precedes procurement,construction and commissioning.','Judicial infrastructure supports access,but case disposal also depends on judges,staff,processes,legal aid and digital reliability.','APshould integrate public transport,barrier-free access,safety and maintenance into the complex.|Measure accessibility and service continuity,not only capital expenditure; no causal fall in pendency is established by a sanction.','Do not call₹547crorethe entire judiciary budget or proof all facilities were completed inJune.','How can court infrastructure investment translate into better access to justice?',src='APCAB',day=4,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','04 · Public guarantees and digital infrastructure','FiberNet financing:₹300croreguarantee is a contingent liability','PTIreports the4JuneCabinet’s financing decision.','The guarantee is toAPPowerFinanceCorporationfor aHUDCOspecial term loan.|Funds are proposed to be transferred toAPStateFiberNetLimited; borrowing entity,guarantor and intended user differ.|A guarantee may create future budget exposure if repayment fails; it is not immediate revenue for all households.','Loan proceeds,government guarantee and grant expenditure are distinct fiscal categories. Digital connectivity requires both network operation and affordable uptake.','APshould disclose debt-service capacity,transfer terms,usage and service-quality improvements.|Compare activated connections,uptime and affordability rather than treat the guaranteed amount as fibre already installed.','Do not add the guarantee and underlying loan as two independent public cash grants or mergeFiberNetwiththe separateBharatNetagreement.','What fiscal and service safeguards should accompany state-backed digital borrowing?',src='APCAB',day=4,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','05 · Organ donation — legal adoption and safeguards','Transplantation oversight:Cabinetapproval before verified ordinance text','The4June report saysAPapproved implementation through an ordinance.','India’s central framework originated in theTransplantationofHumanOrgansAct1994and was amended in2011toinclude tissues.|The contemporary report’sTHOTA2011label should not be mistaken for the original Act’s year.|The stated purpose is stronger oversight and prevention of illegal organ trade; theAPordinanceGazettewas not read.','Consent,authorisation,brain-stem-death certification and protection against commercial dealing involve distinct safeguards; a clinical need does not legitimise trafficking.','APneeds transparent allocation,ethical counselling,regulated hospitals and accessible complaint mechanisms.|Distinguish lawful deceased donation and regulated living donation; avoid inferring all transplants were previously unregulated.','Cabinetapproval is not verified promulgation,commencement or compliance at every hospital. Do not assume a patient automatically receives an organ.','How can organ-transplant regulation protect donors while expanding ethical access?',src='APCAB',day=4,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','06 · Quantum Valley — land and capability','Quantum Valley:registration exemptions are not a working quantum computer','PTIreports the4JuneCabinet’s land-related decision.','The report concerns49.66acresallotted byAPCRDAto theIT/Electronics/CommunicationsDepartment.|Exemptions cover stamp duty,registration fees and other specified registration charges.|Land transfer and fiscal concessions support a project stage; they do not demonstrate research output or operational computing capacity.','Quantum hardware,secure communication,algorithms and workforce development are different capability areas. A project name does not identify a particular validated system.','APshould publish milestones,partner responsibilities,skills plans and access arrangements for universities/start-ups.|Evaluate performance and additionality rather than sum all previously announced national and state commitments as freshJuneinvestment.','Do not confuse49.66acreswithfunding,qubits or completed jobs; the underlying exemption order remains unchecked.','How shouldAPbuild an accountable quantum-technology ecosystem?',src='APCAB',day=4,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','07 · Agricultural energy — land lease and delivery','ChittoorPM-KUSUMproposal:46.69acresis an input,not generation','The4June report records a lease toNREDCAPfor a solar plant.','The reported land is46.69acresinChittoordistrict.|PM-KUSUMis a national agricultural-energy framework with different components; this report does not settle every project-specific component or benefit rule.|Leasing,financial closure,grid connection and operation are distinct stages.','Acreage is notMWcapacity orMWhgeneration. Farmer income effects depend on design,tariff,land rights and reliable payment.','APevaluation should examine agricultural land use,evacuation infrastructure,distribution-company obligations and local consultation.|Do not promise a pump subsidy to every farmer from a reported land-lease decision for a plant.','The primary lease,component approval and project capacity were not read; no commissioned generation is claimed.','What safeguards make agricultural solar investment financially and socially sustainable?',src='APCAB',day=4,ap=True,p='P2')
add('Andhra Pradesh','08 · Tourism PPP — stages and risk allocation','Amaravati Eye:inviting bids underDBFOTdoes not award a concession','PTIreports a4JuneCabinetdecision to invite bids.','The proposed observation-wheel project is on about six acresofAPCRDAland along theKrishna.|DBFOTstands forDesign,Build,Finance,OperateandTransfer.|Bidding,selection,concession agreement,construction,safety certification and operation are separate milestones.','Private financing does not remove public exposure where land,revenue guarantees or termination payments are involved. Demand risk must be allocated explicitly.','APshould test visitor demand,riverbank/floodplain conditions,transport,accessibility and long-term maintenance.|Assess independent structural/operational safety and contract disclosure rather than claim a landmark is already earning tourism revenue.','No selected concessionaire,completed attraction or guaranteed return is established by an invitation to bid.','How should tourismPPPsallocate commercial risk while protecting public land and safety?',src='APCAB',day=4,ap=True,p='P2')
add('Andhra Pradesh','09 · Depositor protection — adjudication and recovery','AgriGoldcases:21special-courtposts are institutional support','The4June report records creation of posts for aVijayawadaspecial court.','The reported court handles cases under theAPProtectionofDepositorsofFinancialEstablishmentsframework andAgriGold-related matters.|Staffing is intended to support speedier disposal; sanctioned posts need actual recruitment and functioning processes.|Case disposal,asset realisation and money returned to depositors are different outcomes.','Attachment secures assets pending lawful process; it is not automatically final confiscation or immediate reimbursement to every claimant.','APshould combine claimant records,transparent asset management and accessible legal assistance.|Measure recovery net of costs,distribution time and inclusion of vulnerable depositors instead of equating staff sanctions with settled claims.','Do not infer all claims have been adjudicated or all investors repaid; no new total recovery figure was verified.','How can special-court capacity strengthen depositor protection without bypassing due process?',src='APCAB',day=4,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','10 · Capital development — Union office project','AmaravatiCGGPOA:₹1,299.08croreUnionofficeapproval','PIB’sJulypublication retrospectively reports the10JuneUnionCabinet/CCEAdecision.','The proposal concernsCentralGovernmentGeneralPoolOfficeAccommodationinAmaravati.|The reported approved cost is₹1,299.08crore; the aim is consolidating central offices and improving coordination.|Construction employment is estimated at seven lakhman-daysper year; this is not seven lakhpermanent jobs.','Capital approval,annual expenditure and completed office occupation are different milestones. Consolidation can reduce fragmentation but needs access and maintenance planning.','APurban analysis should test transport,digital service delivery,water/flood resilience and the opportunity cost of land.|Use the actual10Junedecision date while acknowledging the inspected official narrative was published inJuly.','Do not mistake aUniondecision for a stateCabinetgrant or add prospective man-days as an employee headcount.','How can administrative-capital infrastructure improve public service rather than only real estate activity?',src='AMARAVATI',day=10,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','11 · Capital development — staff housing','AmaravatiGPRA:₹1,234.91croreishousing,not the office complex','The same official account distinguishes a second10Juneapproval.','GeneralPoolResidentialAccommodationis separate fromCGGPOAoffice space.|The reported residential-project cost is₹1,234.91crore.|Its stated objective is reducing staff housing burdens and supporting proximity to work; estimated construction employment is seven lakhman-daysper year.','Office and residential projects can be complementary without being the same asset. Annual man-days cannot be converted to durable jobs without a duration assumption.','Assess inclusive access,transport,service charges and long-term maintenance alongside relocation goals.|The two approved costs sum to₹2,533.99crore; that is a project-cost total,not necessarilyJuneexpenditure.','Do not swap₹1,234.91crorehousing with₹1,299.08croreoffices or claim residents had already moved in on approval.','What makes public employee housing efficient,accessible and fiscally accountable?',src='AMARAVATI',day=10,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','12 · Rural employment — transition to new framework','Juneapproval and1Julystart:preserve the transition date','PTIreportsAPCabinetapproval ofVB–GRAMGimplementation from1July2026.','The reported framework raises the household employment guarantee from100to125days.|Juneapproval,plannedJulystart and actualwork/wage delivery are distinct.|The report mentions faster wages and delayed-payment compensation; detailed final state implementation instruments were not read.','Employment guarantees require demand registration,work allocation,measurement and payment; an annual entitlement is not days already worked.','APshould reconcile ongoing works,old wage liabilities,job cards and grievance channels across the transition.|Evaluate participation,real wages,delay compensation and asset usefulness rather than assume the new title wipes out earlier claims.','Do not report125daysalreadyprovided inJuneor treat a consultation version of central rules as a final state operating rule.','How shouldAPmanage a rural-employment transition without disrupting worker rights?',src='APCAB',day=4,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','13 · Coastal tourism — pilot and regulation','Beach-shackpilot:tourismpermission requires coastal safeguards','The4JuneCabinetreport records draft excise-policy guidelines for pilot beach shacks.','The reported pilot locations areChiralaandVisakhapatnam.|A draft policy/pilot decision differs from permits issued to individual operators.|Excise,land use,coastal regulation,wastewater,safety and public access involve separate approvals.','A state tourism objective does not override coastal-zone restrictions or create unrestricted private rights over the beach.','APshould use transparent selection,seasonal safety plans,waste systems and protection of fishing access.|Evaluate livelihoods,visitor safety and environmental condition; no verified operational shack count or state revenue total is available here.','Do not call every beach eligible or assumeCabinetapprovalaloneauthorises alcohol sales and construction at any coastal site.','How canAPexpand coastal tourism while protecting ecology and community access?',src='APCAB',day=4,ap=True,p='P2')
add('Economy','13 · Mining adjudication — decriminalisation and process','Draft mining inquiries: civil penalties still need due process','PRSrecords aJuneproposal for inquiry/penalty procedures linked toJanVishwaschanges.','The draft concerns prescribed adjudicatory procedures under the mining-law framework.|Replacing selected criminal sanctions with monetary penalties does not legalise the underlying contravention.|Notice,hearing,reasoned findings and appeal are central to fair administrative enforcement.','Decriminalisation,depenalisation and deregulation are different reforms. A civil penalty can remain substantial and enforceable.','APmining administration should prevent selective enforcement and maintain ecological/royalty compliance while simplifying procedure.|Track violation correction and repeat offences; lower criminal exposure should not become a licence for profitable non-compliance.','No final notification,current penalty schedule or automatic immunity for every mining offence is certified by this draft note.','How can decriminalisation improve business certainty without weakening enforcement?',p='P2')
add('Andhra Pradesh','14 · Reorganisation — anniversary and continuing obligations','2June:statehood anniversary is not a new bifurcation','The June compilation recallsTelanganaformation under theAPReorganisationAct2014.','The appointed day was2June2014;2026marks12years since bifurcation.|AndhraState’s1953formation,AndhraPradesh’s1956reorganisation and2014bifurcation are different milestones.|Water,institutions,assets,liabilities and administrative arrangements require issue-specific legal and implementation evidence.','Articles3and4govern formation/reorganisation procedures; an anniversary greeting does not amend statutory obligations or settle inter-state accounts.','APPSCanswers should use a dated timeline and separate legal provisions from negotiated settlements and later litigation.|Link contemporaryTungabhadra/cooperative-federalismdiscussion without claiming every dispute was settled by the2014Act.','Do not callTelanganaIndia’s29thstateas though the current total must still be29; formation-time numbering and current state counts differ.','Why do post-reorganisation disputes require sustained cooperative institutions?',src='DRISHTI',day=2,ap=True,p='P2')
add('Economy','14 · Coal market design — governance and settlement','Coal Exchange Rules: demutualisation and delivery discipline','The rules are dated4June; effect is tied to Gazettepublication,not the9Junewebsite filename.','CoalControllerOrganisationis the defined authority under the reviewed framework.|An exchange applicant must be a company limited by shares and demutualised, separating ownership/management from trading interests.|Registration lasts25years unless revoked/cancelled; a settlement-guarantee fund addresses specified participant defaults.','Market-price discovery requires credible coal quality,sampling,delivery and settlement,not merely an electronic order book. This is not an unrestricted financial-derivatives authorisation.','APthermal-power procurement should assess fuel grade,transport,delivery performance and market concentration.|Governance and conflict-of-interest controls can improve trust; a guarantee fund does not eliminate every commercial or counterparty risk.','Do not equate a rulebook with a fully functioning high-volume exchange or assume25yearsmeansirrevocable registration.','How can coal-exchange design improve transparency without creating new market abuse?',src='PRS,COAL')
